{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he purified the altar</b> — he purged it and cleansed it of foreignness so that it could enter into holiness. <b>And he sanctified it</b> through this service, <b>to make atonement upon it</b> — from now on all atonements [would be effective]. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 8:15). If so, Scripture relates that through this it became sanctified and fit for atonement to be made upon it from here onward. This is like the matter stated in Ezekiel (43:26–27): \"Seven days shall they make atonement for the altar and cleanse it, and they shall consecrate it. And when they have completed the days, it shall be on the eighth day and onward that the priests shall make your burnt-offerings and your peace-offerings upon the altar, and I will accept you — the word of YHWH.\" It teaches here that this was accomplished through the blood, and that the burning of the portions (אֵמוּרִים) is not a disqualifying requirement in the inauguration of the altar, just as for all generations it is not a disqualifying requirement for atonement. However, in the Tosefta of the chapter on the Days of Consecration (Torat Kohanim, Tzav, Millu'im 15), I found [the following]: I do not know what this atonement is. Whence do you say that this atonement was only as Moses said: at the time when the crier went forth to invite donations for the Sanctuary, Israel pressed one another, men and women, and brought [offerings] not of their own free will — let this atonement be so that they would not donate anything stolen to the Sanctuary. And thus it says (Isaiah 61:8): \"For I, YHWH, love justice, I hate robbery in a burnt-offering.\" Rashi also mentioned this in the periculture of 'And you shall command' (Exodus 29:36)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The citation 'תורת כהנים צו מלואים טו' refers to the Sifra on the chapter of Tzav dealing with the days of consecration (millu'im), section 15. The word translated 'disqualifying requirement' renders מְעַכֶּבֶת, literally 'prevents/impedes,' a technical halakhic term."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:48.543954398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}